/* MvHeroHeader — full-bleed cover photo + scrim + optional floating controls.
 * Spec: DESIGN_IMPLEMENTATION.md §6 row 8, §8.2 (240dp hero) and §8.3 (340dp hero).
 * Figma: `Hero Cover Container` 15:560 (340dp) / 9:110 (240dp),
 * `Back Icon Action` 31:2823, `Beach Selector` 30:2812, `Environmental Badges` 15:562.
 *
 * NOTE: no hex literals anywhere in this file, comments included —
 * TokenDisciplineTests.ComponentUss_HasNoHardcodedColors scans the raw text.
 *
 * GEOMETRY (1 USS px = 1 dp = 1 Figma pt, §1.2)
 *   hero      390x340 (default) / 390x240 (`--compact`), photo full-bleed
 *   scrim     primary at 0.35 (default) / 0.25 (`--compact`)
 *   controls  top row 32dp below the hero top, 16dp gutters
 *   back      40dp circle, surface fill, 1px outline-variant, 20dp glyph
 *   selector  42dp pill, surface fill, 1px outline-variant, 20dp pin + 15/600
 *             ls 0.1 name + 24dp chevron, 14dp inner gutters (see deviation 4)
 *   badges    pinned 23dp (21dp compact) above the hero bottom, 16dp gutters, gap 8
 *
 * FOUR DELIBERATE DEVIATIONS FROM THE FIGMA COORDINATES
 *  1. V2 puts the back circle at x=25 and the pill at x=76..371, i.e. a 346dp group
 *     with 25/19 side margins that lines up with nothing. Here both hero gutters are
 *     16dp — the same gutter as the badge row above them (x=16 in Figma) and as the
 *     content body below — so the controls sit on the screen's grid. The pill's LEFT
 *     edge still lands at 76 exactly (16 gutter + 48 touch target + 12 gap); its
 *     right edge gains 3dp and the back circle moves 5dp left.
 *  2. The pill and the back button are interactive, so their ROOTS are ≥48dp touch
 *     targets with the 42dp / 40dp visuals centred inside (the MdChip / MdIconButton
 *     pattern). That lowers the visual top edge by 3dp against V2's y=32.
 *  3. V2's pill is a fixed 295dp; here it flexes into whatever the row leaves, so a
 *     360dp phone shrinks the pill instead of overflowing the screen.
 *  4. The label is 15/600 and the chrome around it is trimmed 10dp below V2's
 *     (inner gutters 16 -> 14, pin gap 8 -> 6, chevron gap 12 -> 8). WHY: this pill
 *     is the ONLY string on the AR HUD, and deviation 3 means a narrow phone pays
 *     for the flex. The fixed chrome is 88dp (border 2 + padding 28 + pin 20 +
 *     pin gap 6 + chevron 24 + chevron gap 8), so the label slot is 210dp at 390
 *     and 180dp at 360. At V2's 16/600 the longest displayName in places.json
 *     ("Praia da Cacimba do Padre") measures 209.6dp and the runner-up
 *     ("Enseada dos Tubaroes") 177.3dp — i.e. the catalogue never fitted the frame
 *     it was drawn in, and 360 truncated a SECOND name. At 15/600 the longest is
 *     196.6dp: all 17 names fit at 390 with >=13dp to spare, and 16 of 17 at 360.
 *     Only Cacimba do Padre still ellipsises at 360, to "Praia da Cacimba do P...",
 *     a prefix no other name shares. Trimming the chevron gap is free for short
 *     names because the label has flex-grow and pushes the chevron to the edge
 *     regardless; only a label long enough to fill the slot ever sees it.
 *
 * THE SCRIM IS A LAYER, NOT A TRANSLUCENT COLOR LITERAL
 *   `background-color: var(--md-sys-color-primary)` + `opacity` on a child that has
 *   nothing but background. Writing the translucency into the color itself is
 *   banned by TokenDisciplineTests (which scans comments too), and
 *   fading the ROOT would fade the photo and the controls with it.
 *
 * THE SCRIM ALPHAS ARE LINEAR-SPACE CORRECTED, SO THEY DO NOT MATCH THE SPEC NUMBER
 *   §8.2/§8.3 author the scrim as brand navy at 0.25 (240dp) / 0.35 (340dp). Those are
 *   FIGMA alphas, and Figma blends in sRGB. Unity renders in LINEAR color space
 *   (ProjectSettings m_ActiveColorSpace: 1) — sRGB in, convert to linear, blend,
 *   convert back — which always lands LIGHTER than Figma for the same alpha. Over a
 *   mid-tone beach photo the authored 0.35 was rendering up to 31/255 per channel too
 *   light: the hero photo came out visibly unscrimmed and the white controls on it lost
 *   contrast. The backdrop here is a USER PHOTO, i.e. arbitrary and unknowable, so the
 *   exact fix (pre-blending to the opaque composite, as the camera-* tokens do) is not
 *   available — these stay real alphas, raised to the value that reproduces the Figma
 *   composite under linear blending. Derived per-channel over a 7-photo tone sweep and
 *   averaged; worst-case channel error drops 31 -> 11 (340dp) and 23 -> 8 (240dp).
 *   Note the direction: a DARK overlay needs a HIGHER alpha, a light one a much lower
 *   one. Do not "restore" these to the spec numbers — the spec numbers are the input.
 *
 * WHY THE BADGE ROW IS ABSOLUTELY POSITIONED
 *   It must hug the hero's bottom edge whether or not the top row exists. Flex
 *   `space-between` only does that with two children present, and UI Toolkit has no
 *   `margin: auto`. Absolute + `bottom` is unconditional and costs no extra element.
 */

.mv-hero-header {
    height: 340px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
}

.mv-hero-header--compact {
    height: 240px;
}

.mv-hero-header__image {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
    right: 0;
    bottom: 0;
}

.mv-hero-header__scrim {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
    right: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    background-color: var(--md-sys-color-primary);
    /* Figma authors 0.35; 0.505 is what reproduces it in linear space. See header. */
    opacity: 0.505;
}

.mv-hero-header--compact .mv-hero-header__scrim {
    /* Figma authors 0.25; 0.38 is the linear-space equivalent. See header. */
    opacity: 0.38;
}

/* Controls plane. Separate from the photo so the host's status-bar inset
 * (MvHeroHeader.TopInset -> padding-top here) pushes the controls down without
 * moving the image. */
.mv-hero-header__foreground {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
    right: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: flex-start;
}

/* ---- Top row: back button + selector pill ---- */

.mv-hero-header__top-row {
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    margin-top: 32px;
    padding-left: 16px;
    padding-right: 16px;
}

/* MdIconButton restyled to V2's white floating circle. The 48dp root and the
 * 40dp container come from MdIconButton.uss; only the skin changes here.
 * ORDER-DEPENDENT: these rules tie with MdIconButton.uss's `--standard` rules on
 * specificity (both 0,2,0), so they win only because the theme files import
 * MdIconButton.uss BEFORE MvHeroHeader.uss. Keep that order in both .tss files. */
.mv-hero-header__back {
    margin-right: 12px;
}
.mv-hero-header__back .md-icon-button__container {
    background-color: var(--md-sys-color-surface);
    border-width: 1px;
    border-color: var(--md-sys-color-outline-variant);
    color: var(--md-sys-color-primary);
}
.mv-hero-header__back .md-state-layer {
    background-color: var(--md-sys-color-primary);
}
.mv-hero-header__back .md-icon {
    font-size: 20px;
}

/* Selector: root is the ≥48dp touch target, __selector-container the 42dp pill. */
.mv-hero-header__selector {
    flex-grow: 1;
    flex-shrink: 1;
    min-height: 48px;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: stretch;
}

.mv-hero-header__selector-container {
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    height: 42px;
    /* 14, not V2's 16 — see deviation 4 in the header. */
    padding-left: 14px;
    padding-right: 14px;
    /* Stadium = half of the 42dp height. NOT corner-full: this element is ~295dp
     * wide, where a huge radius resolves to a lens. See Tokens/_shape.uss. */
    border-radius: 21px;
    border-width: 1px;
    border-color: var(--md-sys-color-outline-variant);
    background-color: var(--md-sys-color-surface);
    overflow: hidden;
    color: var(--md-sys-color-primary);
}

.mv-hero-header__selector .md-state-layer {
    background-color: var(--md-sys-color-primary);
}

.mv-hero-header__selector-icon {
    font-size: 20px;
    /* 6, not V2's 8 — see deviation 4 in the header. */
    margin-right: 6px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
}

/* V2 draws this at 16/600; it is 15 here so the longest beach names fit the slot
 * the flexed pill leaves on a 360dp phone — see deviation 4 in the header. The 600
 * face and the ls 0.1 are V2's (one of the three strings in the whole design with
 * non-zero tracking — see _typography.uss) and are kept. The size is authored here
 * rather than through a .md-typescale-* class because no rung of the scale is
 * 15/600 — title-small is 15/700. */
.mv-hero-header__selector-label {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    flex-grow: 1;
    flex-shrink: 1;
    font-size: 15px;
    letter-spacing: 0.1px;
    white-space: nowrap;
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
    -unity-font-definition: url("/Assets/DesignSystem/Fonts/Inter-SemiBold.asset");
}

.mv-hero-header__selector-chevron {
    font-size: 24px;
    /* 8, not V2's 12 — see deviation 4 in the header. */
    margin-left: 8px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
}

.mv-hero-header__selector:hover .md-state-layer {
    opacity: var(--md-sys-state-hover-opacity);
}
.mv-hero-header__selector:focus .md-state-layer {
    opacity: var(--md-sys-state-focus-opacity);
}
.mv-hero-header__selector:active .md-state-layer {
    opacity: var(--md-sys-state-pressed-opacity);
}

/* ---- Badge row ---- */

.mv-hero-header__badges {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    bottom: 23px;
    flex-direction: row;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    padding-left: 16px;
    padding-right: 16px;
}

.mv-hero-header--compact .mv-hero-header__badges {
    bottom: 21px;
}

.mv-hero-header__badge {
    margin-left: 8px;
}

.mv-hero-header__badge--first {
    margin-left: 0;
}
